                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3c5ea3e4-87f4-3d4d-af96-d491633d6066",
                        "entry_id": "2f290ef7-8bf9-34ca-b8ad-46c2fad4c7b3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To release from smothering."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0b181698-33dc-4560-8e9a-a8cd3e594b46",
                                "sense_id": "3c5ea3e4-87f4-3d4d-af96-d491633d6066",
                                "text": "A tale, a very tale, Angelo ! enter for the love of heaven! enter and unsmother me!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "da7d3103-9cb2-4513-8375-1f4f29ea1755",
                                "sense_id": "3c5ea3e4-87f4-3d4d-af96-d491633d6066",
                                "text": "Write out a conversation of \" smothered thoughts . \" Then \" unsmother ” them ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "be71d7b3-55fa-4902-a8c1-af21e477435a",
                                "sense_id": "3c5ea3e4-87f4-3d4d-af96-d491633d6066",
                                "text": "In addition, we also often insert inactive verb motors in our writing that really drag. We must then both unsmother our verbs and replace them with words that make the sentence move."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "20e736f1-0b3e-4c08-92de-fe26567f880a",
                                "sense_id": "3c5ea3e4-87f4-3d4d-af96-d491633d6066",
                                "text": "No more strangleholds! Ungag our souls!! Unstrangle our souls!! Unsmother our souls!!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "552285f2-3835-4df1-92cd-9c5637c84bee",
                                "sense_id": "3c5ea3e4-87f4-3d4d-af96-d491633d6066",
                                "text": "I am quite smothered with grief, but love requires me to unsmother what unhappiness smothers in me, and my smothered mutterings must be mutedly unsmothered, for I can no longer smother the mutterings I now must unsmother."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d148b4cf-a30b-4a42-874a-d94eb2c3229c",
                                "sense_id": "3c5ea3e4-87f4-3d4d-af96-d491633d6066",
                                "text": "He bent down to unsmother a still-warm vineroot and coaxed it alive."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
